This Elasticsearch 8.19.23 distribution has been modified for MidnightBSD.

The port rebuilds the BSD native-access and entitlement classes from the
matching upstream sources. BSD support is based on the portsbuild/elasticsearch
v9.4.1 changes by Saro, with MidnightBSD platform detection and verified amd64
libc constants. Other upstream classes and multi-release JAR entries are kept. The Java 21
native bindings replace entries in META-INF/versions/21, not the base classes.

The native backend uses the system zstd library and BSD resource limits to
prevent child processes, following Elasticsearch's earlier FreeBSD sandbox.
Native machine learning remains disabled. Vector operations use the upstream
Java fallback; no BSD native vector library is enabled.

The JDK 21 foreign-memory classes are compiled and have their preview class
marker removed in the same way as upstream's MrjarPlugin. Compilation uses
OpenJDK 21; a newer runtime can be selected with elasticsearch_java_home.

Sources:
https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/tree/v8.19.23
https://github.com/portsbuild/elasticsearch/compare/elastic:v9.4.1...v9.4.1
